T1  SCALARIZATION            N=3  beta=2.50   lambda_1=(N^2-1)/(2N)=1.3333   (1/2)Ric=N/8=0.3750
============================================================================================
  C_t = t g^{-1}  =>  Cdot = g^{-1},  Cddot = 0   =>   Cdot Hess V Cdot = Hess V,  -(1/2)Cddot = 0
  (star)  <v,Hess_g V_t v>_g >= lamdot_t  for every g-unit v, every phi, every t>0

  DIMENSION of lamdot_t:  <v,Hess V_t v>_g is dimensionless (v is g-unit, V_t is an action),
  so lamdot_t is DIMENSIONLESS = a curvature FLUX (curvature per unit flow time t).
  t itself is heat time measured in units of g^{-1}, i.e. t = (length)^2 in the physical metric
  g_phys = a^2 g.  Then lam_t is dimensionless, int e^{-2 lam} dt has dimension a^2, so
  gamma = 1/int e^{-2 lam} scales like 1/a^2 = a physical mass^2.  Free field check below.

